#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_wallet
msgid ""
"\n"
"Electronic Wallets\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"A wallet is a prepaid balance held with an issuer -- a fuel-card scheme, a toll\n"
"operator, a meal-voucher provider. This module holds the ledger of it:\n"
"\n"
"* one wallet account per issuer login, mapped to a prepaid asset account of\n"
"  the chart of accounts;\n"
"* the cards (or tags) the issuer handed out, each with its number, holder and\n"
"  latest balance;\n"
"* balance snapshots, one a day once they age;\n"
"* the transactions each card paid for, and the statements the issuer publishes.\n"
"\n"
"It depends on the chart of accounts foundation only. Whoever fills it -- a\n"
"scraper, an import, a hand -- lives in another module, and so does the\n"
"accounting bridge that posts top-ups and consumption once ``account`` is\n"
"installed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_wallet_reorder
msgid ""
"\n"
"Electronic Wallets - Reordering Rules\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"The reordering rule stock keeps per product, kept per wallet card: when a\n"
"card's latest balance falls under its minimum, the amount that brings it\n"
"back to its maximum is ordered from the issuer as a purchase order line for\n"
"the top-up product, one order per wallet account and company. A top-up\n"
"already ordered counts until a balance snapshot dated after it arrives.\n"
msgstr ""

